  "final_answer_preview": "Section 14 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, provides that nothing is an offence if done by a person who believes, in good faith and due to a mistake of fact (not law), that they are legally bound to act. For example, a soldier acting under orders or a court officer mistakenly arresting the wrong person under a court order would not be committing an offence. This section emphasizes the importance of the individual's belief and the nature of the mistake involved.",
